        "title": "Microsoft CEO: We’re moving from OS and apps to agents instead",
        "url": "https://9to5mac.com/2026/06/02/microsoft-ceo-were-moving-from-os-and-apps-to-agents-instead/",
        "content_text": "<div class=\"feat-image\"><img src=\"https://9to5mac.com/wp-content/uploads/sites/6/2026/06/satya-nadella-microsoft-build-2026-1.jpg?quality=82&#038;strip=all&#038;w=1600\" /></div><p class=\"wp-block-paragraph\">Today, Microsoft Build brought the <a href=\"https://www.qualcomm.com/news/onq/2026/06/project-solara-agent-first-computing\">announcement</a> of Project Solara, a new chip-to-cloud platform for AI agents. With the reveal, Microsoft CEO Satya Nadella shared an interesting quote on the company’s vision for an agent-first computing future.</p>\n\n\n\n <a data-layer-pagetype=\"post\" data-layer-postcategory=\"microsoft\" data-layer-viewtype=\"unknown\" data-post-id=\"1054234\" href=\"https://9to5mac.com/2026/06/02/microsoft-ceo-were-moving-from-os-and-apps-to-agents-instead/#more-1054234\" class=\"more-link\">more…</a>",
