        "url": "https://9to5mac.com/2026/06/02/duckduckgo-keeps-surging-on-iphone-after-googles-ai-search-overhaul/",
        "content_text": "<div class=\"feat-image\"><img src=\"https://9to5mac.com/wp-content/uploads/sites/6/2026/05/duckduckgo-no-ai.jpg?quality=82&#038;strip=all&#038;w=1600\" /></div><p class=\"wp-block-paragraph\">DuckDuckGo is riding a <a href=\"https://9to5mac.com/2026/05/26/duckduckgo-sees-iphone-installs-spike-in-the-us-following-ai-announcements-at-google-i-o/\">fresh wave of user interest</a> after Google’s AI-heavy search overhaul demoed at Google I/O. Here’s the latest data on the search engine’s recent success, which is especially strong among iPhone users.</p>\n\n\n\n <a data-layer-pagetype=\"post\" data-layer-postcategory=\"duckduckgo\" data-layer-viewtype=\"unknown\" data-post-id=\"1054229\" href=\"https://9to5mac.com/2026/06/02/duckduckgo-keeps-surging-on-iphone-after-googles-ai-search-overhaul/#more-1054229\" class=\"more-link\">more…</a>",
