        "url": "https://9to5mac.com/2026/06/01/macos-26-5-1-is-out-with-an-important-fix-for-enterprise-users/",
        "content_text": "<div class=\"feat-image\"><img src=\"https://9to5mac.com/wp-content/uploads/sites/6/2026/03/aluminum_header.png?w=1600\" /></div><p class=\"wp-block-paragraph\">Apple just rolled out macOS 26.5.1, which fixes a bug that had been causing Macs with the M5 Apple silicon to unexpectedly shut down under certain conditions. Here are the details.</p>\n\n\n\n <a data-layer-pagetype=\"post\" data-layer-postcategory=\"macos,macos-26,macos-26-5-1\" data-layer-viewtype=\"unknown\" data-post-id=\"1054047\" href=\"https://9to5mac.com/2026/06/01/macos-26-5-1-is-out-with-an-important-fix-for-enterprise-users/#more-1054047\" class=\"more-link\">more…</a>",
