        "title": "Latest Apple Glasses leak has me way more excited for the product",
        "url": "https://9to5mac.com/2026/06/01/latest-apple-glasses-leak-has-me-way-more-excited-for-the-product/",
        "content_text": "<div class=\"feat-image\"><img src=\"https://9to5mac.com/wp-content/uploads/sites/6/2025/05/apple-glasses-light.jpg?quality=82&#038;strip=all&#038;w=1600\" /></div><p class=\"wp-block-paragraph\">Over the weekend, <em>Bloomberg’s</em> Mark Gurman <a href=\"https://9to5mac.com/2026/05/31/apple-glasses-launching-late-2027-with-vision-air-to-follow-by-2029/\">reported</a> that Apple Glasses likely won’t launch until late 2027. But the report also mentions Apple’s planned strategy for its glasses, and it has me way more excited for the product.</p>\n\n\n\n <a data-layer-pagetype=\"post\" data-layer-postcategory=\"apple-glasses\" data-layer-viewtype=\"unknown\" data-post-id=\"1053997\" href=\"https://9to5mac.com/2026/06/01/latest-apple-glasses-leak-has-me-way-more-excited-for-the-product/#more-1053997\" class=\"more-link\">more…</a>",
        "type": "Technology",
        "source": "9to5Mac"
